{'symbol': 'REGN', 'date': '2021-06-04 07:00:00', 'title': 'FDA AUTHORIZES LOWER 1,200 MG INTRAVENOUS AND SUBCUTANEOUS DOSE OF REGEN-COV™ (CASIRIVIMAB AND IMDEVIMAB) ANTIBODY COCKTAIL TO TREAT PATIENTS WITH COVID-19', 'text': 'TARRYTOWN, N.Y., JUNE 4, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0 EUA SUPPORTED BY PIVOTAL PHASE 3 DATA SHOWING 1,200 MG DOSE REDUCED RISK OF HOSPITALIZATION OR DEATH BY 70% ONLY ANTIBODY THERAPY CURRENTLY AVAILABLE IN ALL 50 STATES, INCLUDING EIGHT STATES WITH HIGH RATES OF TWO VARIANTS OF CONCERN REGENERON\xa0PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.\xa0(NASDAQ: REGN) TODAY\xa0ANNOUNCED THE U.S. FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION (FDA) UPDATED THE EMERGENCY USE AUTHORIZATION (EUA) FOR REGEN-COV™, LOWERING THE DOSE TO 1,200 MG (600 MG CASIRIVIMAB AND 600 MG IMDEVIMAB), WHICH IS HALF THE DOSE ORIGINALLY AUTHORIZED.'}